Hi Melanie,

Can you provide a minimal working example? From my end, this process works. Check to see if your genclone object shows that the MLGs represented are filtered (if it says "contracted" multilocus genotypes when you show the object).

Here's an example with the monpop data:

suppressPackageStartupMessages(library(poppr))
data(monpop)
mlg.filter(monpop) <- .Machine$double.eps
monpop
#>
#> This is a genclone object
#> -------------------------
#> Genotype information:
#>
#>    236 contracted multilocus genotypes
#>        (0) [t], (diss.dist) [d], (farthest) [a]
#>    694 haploid individuals
#>     13 codominant loci
#>
#> Population information:
#>
#>      1 stratum - Pop
#>     12 populations defined -
#> 7_09_BB, 26_09_BB, 26_09_FR, ..., 45_10_FR, 26_11_BB, 26_11_FR
length(mlg.id <http://mlg.id>(monpop))
#> [1] 236
mll(monpop) <- "original"
monpop
#>
#> This is a genclone object
#> -------------------------
#> Genotype information:
#>
#>    264 original multilocus genotypes
#>    694 haploid individuals
#>     13 codominant loci
#>
#> Population information:
#>
#>      1 stratum - Pop
#>     12 populations defined -
#> 7_09_BB, 26_09_BB, 26_09_FR, ..., 45_10_FR, 26_11_BB, 26_11_FR
length(mlg.id <http://mlg.id>(monpop))
#> [1] 264
Hope that helps!
Zhian

